# bob-autoinstall.env.example
# Copy this file to bob-autoinstall.env and fill in your values.
# chmod 600 bob-autoinstall.env
#
# bob-autoinstall.sh will refuse to run if bob-autoinstall.env is not present
# or is not restricted to mode 600.
#
# DO NOT commit bob-autoinstall.env to source control — it contains your entitlement key.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# IBM entitlement key for cp.icr.io — all Bob images are now in production.
# Obtain from: https://myibm.ibm.com/products-services/containerlibrary
# Username when using this key: cp
IBM_ENTITLEMENT_KEY="<paste your IBM entitlement key here>"

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bootstrap admin password for bob-admin@bob.ibm.com.
# If unset, bob-autoinstall.sh will prompt interactively.
BOB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""

# Keycloak wait timeout (seconds).
BOB_KEYCLOAK_WAIT_TIMEOUT="120"

# ── IdP Configuration (Optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# A BobIdp CR is REQUIRED for anyone to log in to the Admin UI. The installer
# always creates one unless BOB_SKIP_IDP_CONFIG="true". File selection:
#   1. BOB_IDP_CONFIG, if set
#   2. config-idp.yaml in the install directory, if present
#   3. otherwise a generated baseline: domains [bob.ibm.com],
#      adminEmails [bob-admin@bob.ibm.com]
# To allow other domains (e.g., ibm.com) or LDAP/AD, create config-idp.yaml from
# config-idp-template.yaml. ALWAYS keep bob.ibm.com in domains and
# bob-admin@bob.ibm.com in adminEmails, or you lock out the bootstrap admin.
# OIDC (w3id) is not automated: use the Admin UI at /admin/idp afterwards.
# See docs/04-manual-install.md §11 for details.

# Path to IdP config file (relative to install directory). Empty = auto-detect.
# Example: BOB_IDP_CONFIG="config-idp.yaml"
BOB_IDP_CONFIG=""

# Set to "true" to skip BobIdp creation (NOT recommended: nobody can log in).
BOB_SKIP_IDP_CONFIG="false"

# BobIdp CR ready wait timeout (seconds).
BOB_IDP_WAIT_TIMEOUT="600"